# The org's metrics log is append-only, and since BIN-1362 the sprint commits its own
# review rows into it on the sprint branch. When main gains rows while a sprint runs,
# the sprint's rebase before the push would conflict on two appends at the end of the
# file. `union` keeps both sides' lines, which is the correct merge for this file.
docs/org/metrics/events.jsonl merge=union

# Append-only too, and every branch that records a decision appends its entry at the end of
# the ledger and its heading at the end of the index, so two such branches always met on the
# last line. union duplicates a line both sides added, so read the result after a merge.
.claude/accepted-deviations.md merge=union
.claude/rules/accepted-deviations.md merge=union
